section_context[4]:
  - title: "Runink TIDE Pricing"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/products/tide-pricing/"
    date: "2026-09-27T00:00:00Z"
    description: "What a licence to run Runink TIDE costs. You choose where it runs: on Runink's shared machines, priced per person; in your own cloud account, priced per node; or on your own premises, priced with you. There is no second bill: TIDE never charges a percentage of anything it finds, fixes or ships."
  - title: "Runink FACE"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/products/face/"
    date: "0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    description: "For logistics, freight, claims and operations teams. FACE reads the invoices, orders, carrier records and claim files you already keep, finds the overcharge, the claim about to expire and the broken rule, and drafts the next step for a named person to approve. It runs on your own servers or cloud account, or on Runink's shared machines to start, and no outside AI service is called."
  - title: "Runink PULSE"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/products/pulse/"
    date: "0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    description: "Runink PULSE is marketing software your own team runs: it finds leads, drafts the replies, campaigns and follow-ups, and shows which channel brings customers in. Your team decides what goes out. Priced per seat."
  - title: "Runink TIDE"
    permalink: "https://runink.org/products/tide/"
    date: "0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    description: "Runink TIDE takes the repeat questions off engineering, platform and data teams: what broke and why, whether a fix shipped, which number is right, who changed what. Run it on your own servers, in your own cloud account, or on Runink's shared machines to start. Helpers propose; a person approves."
